3. CORE POPULATION MODEL
============================================================

The fundamental design principle is:

The system does NOT permanently track a fixed set of creator channels.

Instead, for every concept and every extraction day, it constructs a fresh candidate population from YouTube search results.

Concept + extraction date
        ↓
YouTube search
        ↓
raw population
        ↓
filters
        ↓
semantic relevance
        ↓
channel bucketing
        ↓
final population

The final population is whatever number of videos survive ALL required filters.

There is NO requirement that the final population contain exactly 10 videos.

For example:

40 searched
→ 30 after raw filtering
→ 27 after language filtering
→ 21 after semantic filtering
→ FINAL POPULATION = 21

Another day may produce:

40 searched
→ 12 after filtering
→ 8 after semantic filtering
→ FINAL POPULATION = 8

Do not artificially reduce or increase this population to 10.

